  Icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6de92cfe51991c64c90c5eb7f58993cc, type: 3}
  Color: {r: 0.31764707, g: 0.6392157, b: 0.6392157, a: 1}
  Content: The Northern Fibres Guild is a volunteer-driven organiation that fosters
    fibre arts across the Yukon. From spinning and dyeing to weaving,, felting, and
    beading, members explore a wide range of techniques while sharing knowledge and
    creative inspiration. "Fibres of the Land" features the "Climate Stripes Tapestry,"
    a collaborative piece woven during the 2024 Jenni House Residency that visualizes
    climate change in the Yukon through colour and texture. Additional works showcase
    the diversity and talent within the guild today. We hope this exhibition sparks
    our curiosity about fibre arts and the creative community behind them.
  RavenSucessScript: You found ODD Gallery! Strange tastes, sharp eyes. Caw!
  RavenHintScript: "\u201CStamp not showing? Double-check you scanned the right shiny
    square!\u201D"
